# {project_title} — Conventions

This repository was onboarded onto alan with the **ios** stack preset: Swift
6.2 language mode, SwiftUI-first with a closed `enum Route`, The Composable
Architecture (TCA) v1.25.x + swift-dependencies, GRDB v7.x, `URLSession` with
hand-written `Codable`, Swift Testing for units and XCTest for UI flows,
SPM-only dependency management via [Tuist](https://tuist.io/).

## Module map

- `Project.swift` — the Tuist manifest, the only hand-edited project source.
- `Tuist/Package.swift` — external Swift package dependencies.
- `App/Sources/{{AppMain,AppFeature,AppRoute}}.swift`
- `Modules/Domain/` — value types only; imports no framework.
- `Modules/Core/{{Persistence,Networking,DesignSystem,Dependencies,UIKitBridge}}/`
- `Modules/Features/<Feature>/{{Sources,Tests}}/`
- `UITests/`
- `SnapshotTests/` + `__Snapshots__/`
- `.swiftlint.yml`, `.swift-format`, `.periphery.yml`
- `scripts/gate.sh`

## Dependency direction

Compile-enforced by SPM: `Features -> Core -> Domain`. Nothing imports
`Features` except `App`. `Domain` imports nothing. A feature importing a
sibling feature is a build error, not a review comment.

## Placement rules

- Every `UIViewRepresentable`/`UIViewControllerRepresentable` lives in
  `Core/UIKitBridge`.
- Every navigable destination is a case in `AppRoute`.

## Persistence and dependency injection

- GRDB `DatabaseQueue`/`Pool`, migrations and DAOs live in `Core/Persistence`.
- `DependencyKey` with `liveValue`/`testValue`/`previewValue` lives in
  `Core/Dependencies`.

## Coverage

xccov line-coverage floor 0.95. This is line coverage, not branch coverage —
Swift emits no branch-coverage intrinsics.

## Gates (CI, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`)

The `ios-ci` check runs on every pull request and must pass before merge. It
runs the repository's single headless entrypoint, `scripts/gate.sh`.

## Review checklist

1. Did the repository's gate script pass? Red means stop reading.
2. Grep the diff for `@unchecked Sendable` and bare `try?` — the two known
   agent-authorship failure modes that compile clean and pass every gate.
3. Is business logic in a `View` file? Views render, reducers decide.
4. Did a new screen add a case to `AppRoute`?
5. Does every new dependency have a `testValue`?

## Dependencies

Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) opens weekly update pull requests for
both Swift packages (scoped to `Tuist/Package.swift`) and GitHub Actions.
